<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    DEBUG-BUILD-ONLY OVERLAY. Not present in the release APK.

    Purpose: make CameraActivity reachable from `adb shell am start` so a developer can drive the
    synthetic demonstration profile (AnalysisProfile.EXTRA = "demo") through the real camera. There
    is deliberately no in-app way to select a profile - see AnalysisProfile's KDoc: "a mode
    selector the officer can flip is a mode selector that will eventually be flipped in casework."
    Without an external entry point the synthetic profile is unreachable, and an unreachable
    demonstration mode cannot be shown to a reviewer.

    Why an overlay rather than an edit to src/main/AndroidManifest.xml: CameraActivity must stay
    non-exported in release. Exporting it permanently would let ANY app on the device pass the
    profile extra into a case that then reports a demonstration result instead of a field result,
    which is precisely the failure the KDoc above exists to prevent. This overlay keeps the
    release attack surface exactly as it was and confines the widening to debug builds.

    What this does NOT change: capture, ArUco, geometry, rectification, colour measurement, Lab,
    CIEDE2000 and classification are all untouched. Only the reachability of the existing
    "profile" intent extra differs. Field/real mode remains the default for an absent or
    unrecognised extra (AnalysisProfile.indexOf resolves to PROFILE_INDEX_FIELD) and stays
    INCONCLUSIVE.

    tools:replace states the intent that debug wins for this attribute. Without it, adding an
    explicit android:exported="false" to CameraActivity in src/main later would turn this overlay
    into a hard manifest-merge failure instead of the debug-only widening it is meant to be.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <application>
        <activity
            android:name=".CameraActivity"
            android:exported="true"
            tools:replace="android:exported" />
    </application>

</manifest>